## Custom Nodes

- Create custom node components
- Define node types in `nodeTypes` prop
- Use `Handle` component for connection points
- Position handles with `Position` enum
- Style with Tailwind CSS or custom CSS
- Keep nodes simple and focused

### Custom Node Example
```typescript
const CustomNode = ({ data }: NodeProps) => {
  return (
    <div className="px-4 py-2 shadow-md rounded-md bg-white border-2">
      <Handle type="target" position={Position.Top} />
      <div>{data.label}</div>
      <Handle type="source" position={Position.Bottom} />
    </div>
  );
};
```

## Custom Edges

- Create custom edge components
- Define edge types in `edgeTypes` prop
- Use `getBezierPath`, `getSmoothStepPath`, `getStraightPath`
- Add labels with `EdgeText` component
- Implement custom markers
- Handle edge interactions

## Interactivity

### Dragging
- Nodes are draggable by default
- Use `draggable={false}` to disable
- Use `nodesDraggable` for all nodes
- Handle drag events with callbacks

### Selection
- Click to select nodes/edges
- Multi-select with Shift key
- Use `selectable` prop per node/edge
- Style selected state with CSS
- Handle selection changes

### Connection
- Drag from handles to create edges
- Use `onConnect` callback
- Validate connections with `isValidConnection`
- Prevent invalid connections
- Style connection line

